pack federation-runtime-placement
generation control-1
provenance direct filesystem census and live process inspection, 2026-08-26
authority measured
note Runtime placement dimension for the federation. The metric is not Python file count. It is which bodies sit on the hot, standing or effect path with no non-Python realization. Implementation convenience does not confer semantic or runtime ownership.

census cen:runtime-composition
  measured_at 2026-08-26
  scope Documents/Bonfyre, excluding node_modules, .git and frappe-bench
  python_files_total 1012
  python_files_vendored 569
  python_files_authored 443
  correction a raw count of 1012 overstates the surface by more than half; 569 files are site-packages under services/bonfyre-restate-adapter/venv
  c_files 308
  c_headers 93
  zig_files 4
  javascript_files 22
  typescript_files 5
  rust_files 10
  perl_files 5
  shell_files 178
  authored_python_by_area components 220, services adapter, scripts 32, tools 18, cmd 12, architecture 10
  components_split 143 non-test, 77 tests
  note C remains the largest native body count; the Python surface is large but roughly half vendored and roughly a third tests

finding fnd:python-owns-the-effect-path
  severity high
  state VERIFIED_BY_MEASUREMENT
  claim the two live Python processes that matter are not tooling; they own the effect path
  evidence process 890 runs /Users/nickgonzales/.bonfyre/mcp/project_node.py under python 3.9
  evidence process 8966 runs /Users/nickgonzales/.bonfyre/agents-runtime/operator_agents_runtime.py under python 3.12
  evidence process 879 runs an agent hypervisor canary server under python 3.12
  detail project_node.py serves project_read, project_search, project_patch_preview, project_apply_patch, project_apply_low_risk_patch, project_commit_receipt, project_revert_receipt and project_test_profile
  consequence the machinery that mutates client source is Python-owned with no alternative realization
  detail operator_agents_runtime.py executes autonomous goals against that carrier
  consequence the machinery that decides and drives autonomous work is Python-owned with no alternative realization
  scary_metric HOT_OR_EFFECT_PATH and PYTHON_ONLY equals 2 live bodies
  contrast a thousand Python archaeology scripts would be nearly irrelevant; these two are not

finding fnd:dependency-blocks-the-machine
  severity high
  state VERIFIED_BY_MEASUREMENT
  claim the operator's Python dependency stack is what has blocked 86 goals all session
  evidence every operator run fails on ValidationError for InputTokensDetails.cache_write_tokens
  mechanism a pydantic model version mismatch inside the Python agent runtime
  significance this is the concrete cost of accidental runtime ownership; a library version in a convenience runtime is holding the autonomous lane down
  relation_to_ladder carrier admission fails while capability and body both exist
  note recorded here because the cause is runtime placement, not the operator's design

