body_role bdr:scaling-substrates
  body .bonfyre/run8/canonical/estate/.../TOOLS/scaling_substrate/*.py
  runtime_family Python
  role REFERENCE_IMPLEMENTATION
  detail five modules, 12 of 12 checks passing under python 3.12
  disposition PRESERVE as reference; the described substrates are meant to be dense native execution units, and a passing Python reference is exactly the right proving artifact
  caution do not mistake a passing reference implementation for the native realization the design calls for

representation_selection rs:exact-sets
  finding four distinct exact-set representations exist and are probably not duplicates
  candidate BitRegistry in current source, a machine-word mask over a small fixed universe
  candidate SparseBitmap in the canonical substrate, a sparse-set physical representation
  candidate a native ROBDD in the canonical substrate, a compiled Boolean admission predicate
  candidate ExecutableClosureIndex in the canonical substrate, a maintained hot closure lookup
  proposed_rule tiny fixed universe uses a machine-word mask; moderate sparse closure uses a sparse bitmap; a complex Boolean admission predicate uses a decision diagram; a frequently demanded executable closure uses the hot index; a cold or open-world closure uses a query
  invariant this is representation selection for exact sets, measured per demand, not a choice of one winner
  supersedes the earlier framing that two bitmap systems were unaware duplicates

admission_rule ar:implementation-convenience
  rule implementation convenience does not confer semantic or runtime ownership
  procedure before creating a new runtime owner, search native commands, shared libraries, current operating machinery, preserved implementations, specialized runtimes and lower substrates
  default_disposition REFERENCE_IMPLEMENTATION, WRAP_ADAPTER or PATCH_EXISTING_OWNER
  prohibited NEW_RUNTIME_OWNER by default
  applies_equally Python convenience, a new service, a rewrite in a preferred language, a new state store, a new daemon, a new index, a new API wrapper
  agent_bias_note the rule is about any implementer's convenient environment, not one language

disposition_ring1 ExecutionFrame
  do_not write a new module
  instead compose the six dimensions from existing owners and pass a small immutable packed value through the execution fabric
  pending_search authority.py, execution_environment.py and any world or frontier fields in current source

disposition_ring1 StandingAddress
  do_not write a new service
  instead connect an address query, a read closure, a current relation, incremental invalidation and the hot index
  note the parts exist separately; the behavior does not

disposition_ring1 SemanticConstraintNetwork
  do_not build the diagram literally
  instead inventory ConstraintIR, the planner, the decision diagram, the capability hypergraph, AllocationProblem, authority masks and provider constraints
  hypothesis the network is a compiled projection over existing specialized constraint sources

era_note
  era_a native and low level: C, Zig, packed bodies, native commands, hot indexes, binary formats
  era_b runtime and product: Bun, JavaScript, provider integrations, projection surfaces
  era_c reconstruction and control plane: architecture census, semantic models, validators, tests, institutional modelling
  error treating era C as if it superseded A and B
  correct era C explains, tests and federates A and B, and owns runtime machinery only with an explicit reason
  historical_constraint later native work established a native runtime owner with C acceleration, making earlier Python expansion capture and source material rather than final runtime ownership
